# README — REQ-001

## Scope
REQ-001 implements the canonical PostgreSQL schema backbone for Documentale v1.

Delivered in this iteration:
- versioned PostgreSQL up/down migrations for `documents`, `review_decisions`, `audit_events`, and `idempotency_records`
- database-enforced document lifecycle constraints for the allowed transitions
- canonical domain contract modules for document lifecycle, document record fields, review decision values/shape, audit action/entity names, and idempotency persistence shape
- a minimal repository contract seam under `src/platform/db` so later REQs can reuse one persistence vocabulary rather than re-derive it from SQL
- unit and integration tests proving migration apply, replayability, foreign-key integrity, enum enforcement, lifecycle transition enforcement, terminal-state protection, data-quality checks, and idempotency uniqueness

Not delivered in this iteration:
- HTTP routes
- OIDC middleware
- AWS deployment descriptors
- business handlers beyond schema and contract support

Implementation decisions were informed by the local source snapshot and project artifacts provided for this run.

## Files Emitted
- `runs/kit/REQ-001/src/src/platform/db/migrations/0001_req_001_canonical_schema.sql`
- `runs/kit/REQ-001/src/src/platform/db/migrations/0001_req_001_canonical_schema.down.sql`
